# P0 · Foundation and safety · Weeks 1–3 · R0 Internal platform
# exit: 1 journeys sign-off · 2 restore tested+timed · 3 cross-tenant RLS test · 4 CI green + staging deploy from tag
# nfr:  1 OWASP ASVS L2 · 2 PHI-redacted structured logs · 3 daily encrypted backup + PITR
# pkg:  1 staging URL + seeded synthetic tenant · 2 ADR set, threat model, role matrix, data map · 3 R0 release notes
# dep:  1 Azure subscription + launch region · 2 founder decision on launch market (ADR-002)

@epic MDV-P0-E01 | Repository, CI/CD and environments | P0-01, P0-02 | A deployable .NET 10 + React monorepo with green CI and tagged deploys to staging.
@epic MDV-P0-E02 | Identity, tenancy and authorisation | P0-03, P0-04, P0-05 | Staff sign in with MFA into the right facility and only see what their role allows, enforced on the server and in SQL.
@epic MDV-P0-E03 | Audit, data security and observability | P0-06, P0-09, P0-10 | Every patient-data access is provable; national IDs are unreadable to admins; nothing sensitive leaks into logs.
@epic MDV-P0-E04 | Design system and journeys | P0-07 | The Medvya theme, clinical primitives and i18n/RTL pipeline in code; the six journeys signed off.
@epic MDV-P0-E05 | Safety, compliance groundwork and R0 gate | P0-08, P0-10 | Decisions, threat model, data map, DPIA and policies recorded; R0 handed over.

=== MDV-P0-001
title: Create the Medvya monorepo skeleton (Medvya.sln, web workspaces, packages)
type: Task
epic: MDV-P0-E01
prd: P0-01
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: platform, repo
estimate: 1
weeks: 1
depends: MDV-P0-002
confidence: 92 | Layout fully specified by PRD v2 §07 and docs/03-architecture/repository-structure.md.
sources: PRD v2 §07 Repository; docs/03-architecture/repository-structure.md
desc:
Create the repository layout agreed in ADR-001: Medvya.sln with src/Host.Api, src/BuildingBlocks/*, src/Modules/<Module>/{Domain,Application,Infrastructure,Api} for the P0 modules (Identity, Tenancy, Audit), src/Workers/Worker.Jobs, web/clinic, web/portal (placeholder), packages/{ui,api-client,i18n,test-fixtures}, tests/*, infra/bicep, docs, tools.
Pin the .NET 10 SDK (global.json), central package management (Directory.Packages.props), nullable + warnings-as-errors + analyzers (Directory.Build.props), pnpm workspaces for web/* and packages/*.
ac:
- Given a fresh clone, when I run `dotnet build` and `pnpm install && pnpm -r build`, then both succeed with zero warnings.
- The folder layout matches docs/03-architecture/repository-structure.md for every folder needed in P0; later modules are not created yet.
- global.json pins a .NET 10 SDK; Directory.Packages.props holds every NuGet version; no project file contains a version number.
- web/clinic starts with `pnpm --filter clinic dev` on React 19 + TypeScript + Vite and renders a placeholder page using packages/ui.
- README.md explains prerequisites, local start and links to docs/; AGENTS.md states the synthetic-data-only and no-PHI-in-logs rules.
tests:
- CI job builds the solution and the web workspace on a clean runner.

