sources: PRD v2 P0-10, finding "ERD and Build Plan assume PostgreSQL", completeness "ERD mapped to Azure SQL types"; docs/03-architecture/data-model.md
desc:
Produce docs/03-architecture/data-classification.md listing every planned field for P0–P2 entities with its class (public, internal, personal, sensitive health, national ID) and control (RLS, masking, Always Encrypted, audit-on-read). Finalise the ERD → Azure SQL mapping (uuid → uniqueidentifier, jsonb → json/nvarchar(max)+ISJSON, exclusion constraint → unique slot index + app lock, RLS policies → security predicates, money → bigint minor units). Add a [Classification] attribute in code used by the PHI redaction processor and EF configuration.
ac:
- Every column in the P0 schema has a classification attribute; a unit test fails if a new entity property lacks one.
- The register lists the Always Encrypted column set and the masking set used by MDV-P0-009.
- The mapping table closes the PRD completeness item "ERD mapped to Azure SQL types" (status Covered).
- The data map (what data, where stored, which country, which processors) is published as part of the P0 delivery package.

=== MDV-P0-017
title: Append-only audit log on Azure SQL ledger tables with audit middleware
type: Story
epic: MDV-P0-E03
prd: P0-06
priority: MUST
roles: Practice admin, System
labels: audit, ledger
estimate: 2.5
weeks: 2-3
depends: MDV-P0-010, MDV-P0-016
confidence: 85 | Requirement explicit; ledger table behaviour with EF Core needs a small proof (append-only ledger is supported).
sources: PRD v2 P0-06, §07b layer 08; docs/adr/ADR-006-immutable-signed-records.md
desc:
AUDIT_EVENT as an append-only ledger table: actor, tenant, facility, patient ref (opaque id), action, resource ref, purpose, outcome (allowed/denied), timestamp, IP, correlation id — no PHI values. A mediator behaviour and endpoint filter write an event for every read and write of patient data, sign-in, export and permission change. Ledger digests are exported daily to immutable Blob and verified by a scheduled job.
ac:
- Every endpoint tagged as patient-data read or write produces exactly one audit event per request (test enumerates endpoints).
- The app identity cannot UPDATE or DELETE audit rows (permission test); ledger verification detects a tampered row in a test database.
- Audit events contain opaque patient ids only; a test scans payloads for names, phone numbers and identifiers and fails if found.
- Daily digest export to an immutable (time-based retention) container succeeds and verification runs on schedule with an alert on mismatch.
- Denied authorization attempts are audited with outcome "denied".

=== MDV-P0-018
title: Observability with OpenTelemetry and PHI redaction (structured logs, telemetry processor)
type: Task
epic: MDV-P0-E03
prd: P0-10
covers: nfr:2
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: observability, privacy
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 2
depends: MDV-P0-016
confidence: 88 | Explicit NFR; implementation pattern known.
sources: PRD v2 P0 NFR 2, X2, X8; docs/03-architecture/README.md#trust-boundaries-software-architecture-2
desc:
OpenTelemetry tracing/metrics/logs → Application Insights. A telemetry processor drops request/response bodies, query strings, auth headers, blob URLs and any field marked sensitive by the classification attribute. Structured logging with message templates only (no string-concatenated values of classified fields). Front-end error reporting strips URLs with ids and never sends form values.
ac:
- A test request containing a synthetic patient name, phone and Emirates ID produces telemetry in which none of those values appear (automated log scan in integration tests).
- Request bodies and query strings are never exported; correlation ids are.
- Dashboards show request rate, p95 latency, error rate and dependency failures for staging.
- An alert fires on 5xx rate > 2 % over 5 minutes in staging/prod.

=== MDV-P0-019
title: Backups, point-in-time restore and a timed restore drill
type: Task
epic: MDV-P0-E01
prd: P0-02
covers: nfr:3, exit:2
priority: MUST
roles: Developer
labels: backup, dr
estimate: 1
weeks: 3
depends: MDV-P0-006
confidence: 90 | Azure SQL PITR is built in; drill is a runbook exercise.
sources: PRD v2 P0 NFR 3, exit 2, X7; docs/04-security-compliance/README.md
desc:
Configure PITR retention (35 days in prod), long-term retention per country rule, backups kept in-country; storage soft delete/versioning for Blob. Write runbook docs/runbooks/restore.md and perform one restore of staging to a new database, verifying data and timing.
ac:
- PITR and LTR settings are defined in Bicep, not set by hand.
- A restore drill of staging completes and the elapsed time is recorded in the runbook (P0 exit gate 2).
- Restored database passes a smoke test (row counts per table match the point in time).
- Backup storage redundancy keeps data in-country (no geo-replication outside the country).

=== MDV-P0-020
title: Medvya design system in code: MUI theme, tokens and clinical status primitives (packages/ui)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P0-E04
prd: P0-07
priority: MUST
roles: All
labels: design-system, ui
estimate: 3
weeks: 1-2
depends: MDV-P0-001
confidence: 92 | Theme is given verbatim in Handoff and component states are fully specified.
sources: docs/02-design/tokens.md; docs/02-design/components-theme-copy.md
desc:
packages/ui exports the Medvya MUI theme (verbatim from Handoff, plus the `ai` palette via module augmentation and dark tokens prepared but off) and the clinical primitives: Button states (default/hover/focus/loading/disabled with count), StatusChip (ordered/received/reviewed/completed, icon + label), ProvenanceTag (AI draft · not reviewed dashed violet / Verified / Synced from HIS / Patient reported / Imported / Signed), Alert (critical/attention/info with words), TextField states, RecordingPill (REC/paused/declined), IdentityBanner (name, age, sex, MRN, DOB, allergies never collapsed, consent, encounter, SYNTHETIC marker). A storybook-like gallery page in web/clinic (/__ui) shows every state.
ac:
- Theme values (palette, typography, shape 10, spacing 8, breakpoints xs 0/sm 360/md 768/lg 1280/xl 1600, MuiButton minHeight 44 and no text-transform, MuiPaper 1px #DFE7ED border no shadow, tabular-nums in tables) match docs/02-design/components-theme-copy.md exactly.
- Every primitive renders all states listed in Handoff §1; no status is conveyed by colour alone (icon + text present, checked by test).
- Focus ring is 2px #2563EB with 2px offset on all interactive primitives.
- axe reports no violations on the gallery page; text contrast of tokens matches the Foundations ratios (≥ 4.5:1 for text).
- prefers-reduced-motion disables animation in RecordingPill/progress.

=== MDV-P0-021
title: Internationalisation pipeline: English, Hindi, Arabic with full RTL
type: Task
epic: MDV-P0-E04
prd: P0-07
priority: MUST
roles: All
labels: i18n, rtl
estimate: 1.5
weeks: 2
depends: MDV-P0-020
confidence: 88 | Requirement explicit (X5); translations themselves need human review later.
sources: PRD v2 P0-07, X5; docs/02-design/responsive-and-dark.md#rtl-and-languages
desc:
packages/i18n with ICU message format, keys from Handoff microcopy (ai.badge, note.signBlocked, consent.declined, result.received, msg.delivered, pay.pending, ai.unavailable, err.403, push.generic …). Locale switch en/hi/ar; Arabic switches MUI to RTL (stylis RTL plugin, logical properties), Noto Sans Arabic font, flipped directional icons. Brand name "Medvya" comes from a single key so the working name can be replaced globally.
ac:
- Switching to Arabic flips layout direction for the whole app shell and the gallery without visual overlap (Playwright screenshot test at 360 and 1280 px).
- No user-facing string is hard-coded in components (lint rule fails on JSX text literals outside i18n).
- Missing translation keys fall back to English and are reported in CI.
- Handoff microcopy keys exist with the exact English text from docs/02-design/components-theme-copy.md.
- Numbers, dates and currency format per locale and country (₹ with Indian grouping, AED).

