desc:
tools/synthetic-data-generator and packages/test-fixtures produce the synthetic cast (Iyer Family Clinic, Dr. Arjun Rao, A. Joseph, S. Thomas RN, Priya N., Meera Iyer, Deepak Nair; a UAE tenant Al Noor Family Clinic with Dr. Omar Haddad and Fatima Al Mansoori) with users for every role. Staging is seeded on deploy; data is visibly marked SYNTHETIC.
ac:
- Staging has a seeded India tenant with one user per role (and a UAE tenant if parameters enabled) able to sign in with MFA.
- All seeded records carry a synthetic marker and use invalid-by-construction identifiers (e.g. ABHA/EID numbers that fail real checksums).
- Re-seeding is idempotent and never runs against production (guarded by environment check + test).
- The staging URL and seed accounts are listed in the R0 delivery package (secrets shared out of band).

=== MDV-P0-028
title: Per-tenant feature flags with owner and kill switch
type: Task
epic: MDV-P0-E01
prd: P0-04
priority: MUST
roles: Developer, Medvya operations
labels: feature-flags
estimate: 1
weeks: 3
depends: MDV-P0-010
confidence: 85 | Required by release process §08 and X8; simple table-backed implementation suffices until P5 ops console.
sources: PRD v2 §08 Feature flags, X8
desc:
Feature flags stored per tenant (flag key, enabled, owner, created/changed by, audit). Evaluated server-side and exposed in /v1/me/context; UI hides routes and nav items for disabled flags; API rejects calls to disabled features with 404. Flags can be turned off without redeploy.
ac:
- Turning a flag off hides the feature for that tenant within one minute without redeploy.
- Every flag has an owner and description; flag changes are audited.
- API endpoints behind a disabled flag return 404 (not 403) and are not listed in the tenant's navigation.
- Flags default to off for new features.

